using System.Diagnostics;

namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_RemoveContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
            // ... assume preconditions and other setup code ...

            arrList.Remove(x);

            // ... observe values and other post-conditions ...

            // @@@ the last position of x in old array is greater than or equal to some position of x in the same array
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= arrList.LastIndexOf(x));
        }
    }
}
```

The `Debug.Assert` statement is used to perform runtime checks for conditions that should always be true during the execution of the program. In the given code, the `Debug.Assert` statement is used to check whether the last position of `x` in the old array is greater than or equal to the current last position of `x` in the same array after removing `x` from the array. This ensures that the precondition that the last position of `x` in the old array is greater than or equal to the some position of `x` in the same array is always satisfied.--------------------```cs
